Package: SparseMSE
Title: 'Multiple Systems Estimation for Sparse Capture Data'
Version: 2.0.2
Authors@R: c(
  person("Lax", "Chan", email = "laxchan77@gmail.com", role = c("aut")),
  person("Bernard W.", "Silverman", email = "bernard.silverman@stats.ox.ac.uk", role = c("aut","cre")),
  person("Kyle", "Vincent", email = "kyle.shane.vincent@gmail.com", role = c("aut")))
Description: Deprecated package. Users should use 'MultipleSystemsEstimation'
    instead of 'SparseMSE'. 'MultipleSystemsEstimation' includes the functionality
    of 'SparseMSE' and extends it with additional methods and documentation.
    'SparseMSE' implements multiple systems estimation methods for sparse capture
    data, including cases with non-overlapping lists and boundary estimates. The
    methods were developed and analysed by Chan, Silverman and Vincent (2019)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1902.05156>.
URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.05156
